<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  fleet-collect — ingest Claude Code transcripts into ~/dev/.fleet/fleet.db every 2 min.

  Install (opshost only — the ledger host). The log directory must exist first:
  launchd does not create it, and a missing StandardOutPath silently prevents the
  job from starting.
    mkdir -p ~/dev/.fleet
    cp launchd/org.eunomia.fleet-collect.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.eunomia.fleet-collect.plist
  Reload after editing (a frozen daemon needs bootout+bootstrap, not just kickstart):
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/org.eunomia.fleet-collect
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.eunomia.fleet-collect.plist

  ProgramArguments uses an absolute path because launchd does not read a login shell.
  Replace /Users/operator with the real home if this is ever installed elsewhere.

  RUNS FROM THE PINNED WORKTREE, not ~/dev/eunomia. Until 2026-09-07 this unit
  executed the shared clone, so every 120 seconds it ran whatever branch a
  session had last left checked out there. That clone was observed on three
  different branches in one afternoon. It is the same defect fleet-secret-guard
  had (fixed by pinning) and the same one fleet-watch now reports as `pin-drift`.
  A scheduled job is the worst place for it: nobody is watching when it fires.

  The pin is a detached worktree of this repo at ~/.local/share/pins/eunomia. It
  is the pinned eunomia deployment, shared by several units and the PreToolUse
  hook. It was called fleet-guard until 2026-09-07, when both pins were
  collected under ~/.local/share/pins/<repo>.
  Updating it is deliberate: fetch, then checkout with the detach flag onto
  origin/main. (MOVING it to another path is a different operation with its
  own procedure — see bin/fleet-secret-guard.) fleet-watch reports when it falls behind.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>org.eunomia.fleet-collect</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/operator/.local/share/pins/eunomia/bin/fleet-collect</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>120</integer>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Collection is a read-only sweep of transcripts; it must never delay a login
       or contend with an active session. Background QoS keeps it off the critical path. -->
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>
  <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
  <true/>
  <key>Nice</key>
  <integer>5</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/operator/dev/.fleet/collect.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/operator/dev/.fleet/collect.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
